            {
              "id": "e07c1b26-b136-44c6-8815-981ccadf288c",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>Children's Games &amp; Rhymes</strong></em> is a collection of essays edited by Paul G. Brewster, published by Duke University Press in 1952."
            },
            {
              "id": "a3d37546-c735-41cc-91b7-edaf89518dc0",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "c6963f72-e2ff-4de2-b3d7-e6cac4914a9f",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>Examines and explains the folklore for many types of games such as ball games; hiding games; jumping and hopping games; practical jokes; battle games; dramatic games; guessing games; forfeit or penalty games; games of chase; games of dexterity and imitative games.</em>"
            }
          ]
        },
